    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0325" n="227" xml:id="pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/419: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-03T14:00:00-04:00">September 3, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Your 223, September 2, 5 p.m. In case the Japanese Government communicates
                    to you the text of a so-called treaty between Japan and “Manchoukuo”, please
                    report that fact immediately to the Department and take no other action even of
                    acknowledgment pending receipt of further instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rogers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
